		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: COCOTO SURPRISE uses Bullet physic engine.]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=24421#p24421"><![CDATA[
The new Bullet Physics engine has been integrated into Blender and <a href="http://originalcialis.com" class="postlink">cialis</a> allows for rigid body physics simulations within the game engine. The engine allows objects to fall, roll, and collide with other objects in a realistic manner. It is an ongoing development process, but currently very much in a usable state.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=8467">workaholic_4</a> — Mon Jul 25, 2011 12:44 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
