		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=16521#p16521"><![CDATA[
COCOTO SURPRISE uses Bullet physic engine.<br><br>Available for Nintendo Wii from 27 November, 2009.<br>Publisher: Neko Entertainment.<br>Distributor: Bigben Interactive. <br>PEGI: 3+<br><br>Go fishing for gifts!<br><br>Play either one of the 4 characters of Cocoto’s world and go fishing for treasures in one of the 4 magical environments of this famous series: Abyss, Atlantis, Jungle and Heaven. Watch out, each world will have its own challenges and gifts!<br><br>Fishing rod Wii in hand, the player has to catch most possible presents by showing a lot of address and precision, but also craftiness to chase away all the hidden surprises.<br><br>Every present contains a true interactive surprise: meuh box, automaton, spring balls,  tens of toys to be collected, to be assembled, to manipulate in the infinity!<br><br>It will be necessary to thwart the traps of every universe to catch the presents which will delight Fairy, the small friendly fairy of Cocoto.<br><br>The gifts’ fishing is a theme which will remind numerous souvenirs to all the family, such fishes for ducks when they were small. Just like a kids’ room, the toy box is filled with all the interactive presents got back in the sinned presents. The children can play with during hours.<br><br>Key points<br>•A in-house physic engine using Bullet Collision Detection.<br>•Innovatives physic &amp; rendering engines who allow: shader, dynamic shadow, fluid, never seen on the Nintendo Wii -&gt; Attractive gameplay and beautiful graphics.<br>•4 Fantastic worlds: Jungle, Abyss, Atlantis, Heaven.<br>•80 levels matching with 80 treasures to catch among which some have several parts to assemble.<br>•100 interactive gifts: music box, balloons, bells, snow balls, lens cards, etc.<br>•4 hours of gameplay to fish all treasures but hours of fun with the interactive gifts.<br>•Up de 4 players.<dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/download/file.php?id=378" class="postimage" alt="We made a video for Bullet web site 8 )&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Video url:&lt;br /&gt;http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IAQ52fXxXdQ&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Video integration:&lt;br /&gt;&amp;lt;object width=&amp;quot;425&amp;quot; height=&amp;quot;344&amp;quot;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;param name=&amp;quot;movie&amp;quot; value=&amp;quot;http://www.youtube.com/v/IAQ52fXxXdQ&amp;amp;hl=fr_FR&amp;amp;fs=1&amp;amp;rel=0&amp;quot;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/param&amp;gt;&amp;lt;param name=&amp;quot;allowFullScreen&amp;quot; value=&amp;quot;true&amp;quot;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/param&amp;gt;&amp;lt;param name=&amp;quot;allowscriptaccess&amp;quot; value=&amp;quot;always&amp;quot;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/param&amp;gt;&amp;lt;embed src=&amp;quot;http://www.youtube.com/v/IAQ52fXxXdQ&amp;amp;hl=fr_FR&amp;amp;fs=1&amp;amp;rel=0&amp;quot; type=&amp;quot;application/x-shockwave-flash&amp;quot; allowscriptaccess=&amp;quot;always&amp;quot; allowfullscreen=&amp;quot;true&amp;quot; width=&amp;quot;425&amp;quot; height=&amp;quot;344&amp;quot;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/embed&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/object&amp;gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Cheers." onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1715">fred</a> — Mon Dec 14, 2009 2:12 pm</p><hr />
